From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:51:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbx: report an unknown USB type while
 APSD runs

Reading POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_USB_TYPE returns -EAGAIN until automatic power
source detection (APSD) has finished. power_supply_uevent() only skips a
property that fails with -ENODEV, -ENODATA or -EINVAL; any other error
fails the whole uevent. With a cable attached at boot, APSD is usually
still running when udev triggers the coldplug "add" event, so the
charger's event is dropped:

  power_supply pmi8998-charger: uevent: failed to send synthetic uevent: -11

and reading usb_type from sysfs fails with EAGAIN in the same window.

While detection runs the type simply isn't known yet, which is what
POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_UNKNOWN means. Report that, as other chargers
with BC1.2 detection do (bq256xx, bq25630, mp2629). The driver's status
work already polls for the APSD result and calls power_supply_changed()
once it is in, so userspace still gets the real type.

The status work keeps using -EAGAIN internally to retry and rerun APSD.

Fixes: 8648aeb5d7b7 ("power: supply: add Qualcomm PMI8998 SMB2 Charger driver")
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index f5ebf07886..f58c51ad92 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -659,6 +659,7 @@ static int smb_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 			     union power_supply_propval *val)
 {
 	struct smb_chip *chip = power_supply_get_drvdata(psy);
+	int rc;
 
 	switch (psp) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MANUFACTURER:
@@ -682,7 +683,16 @@ static int smb_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_HEALTH:
 		return smb_get_prop_health(chip, &val->intval);
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_USB_TYPE:
-		return smb_apsd_get_charger_type(chip, &val->intval);
+		rc = smb_apsd_get_charger_type(chip, &val->intval);
+		/*
+		 * APSD is still running. The type isn't known yet, and
+		 * smb_status_change_work() reports it once APSD is done.
+		 */
+		if (rc == -EAGAIN) {
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_UNKNOWN;
+			return 0;
+		}
+		return rc;
 	default:
 		dev_err(chip->dev, "invalid property: %d\n", psp);
 		return -EINVAL;
